@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-fees-regs`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s63-commencement`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s6-second-schedule`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s8-validity`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s2-s3-licensing-duty`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s7-s9-exemption-and-temporary-licence`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s16-s17-duties-of-licensee`
IMPORT `hvac-tests-calendars`

-- hvac-tests-law.l4 -- tests for ss 2, 3, 6 and the Second Schedule, 7, 8, 9, 16, 17 and 63.
--
-- Expected values come from the text each section cites, not from the code.  Where a boundary
-- depends on a reading registered in NOTES.md as a fork, the comment says which (F-xx): those
-- assertions show what the TAKEN reading answers, not what the Law compels.

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 63: Commencement`
-- ============================================================================

#ASSERT `the day the Law was published` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 14

-- Reading B (taken): the later of 14 April 2025 and 16 July 2025.
#ASSERT `the Commencement Day` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- Reading A: three months after 16 July 2025.
#ASSERT `the Commencement Day on the other reading` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
-- The two readings differ, so the fork is real (F-C1).
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commencement Day` EQUALS `the Commencement Day on the other reading`)

`a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`     MEANS Refrigerant OF TRUE,  TRUE
`a listed flammable refrigerant, use not permitted` MEANS Refrigerant OF TRUE,  FALSE
`an ordinary refrigerant`                           MEANS Refrigerant OF FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the class of work for commencement of` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted` EQUALS `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law`
-- s 63(a)(2) takes the rest, including a listed refrigerant whose use the law does not permit (F-C2).
#ASSERT `the class of work for commencement of` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use not permitted` EQUALS `work on a system using any other refrigerant`
#ASSERT `the class of work for commencement of` `an ordinary refrigerant` EQUALS `work on a system using any other refrigerant`

-- s 63(a)(1): the Commencement Day itself.  s 63(a)(2): 18 months from it.
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

#ASSERT NOT `the Law is in force on` (YMD 2025 7 15) `for work on a system using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`
#ASSERT `the Law is in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `for work on a system using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`
#ASSERT NOT `the Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 1 15) `for work on a system using` `an ordinary refrigerant`
#ASSERT `the Law is in force on` (YMD 2027 1 16) `for work on a system using` `an ordinary refrigerant`
#ASSERT NOT `the Law is in force on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `for work on a system using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use not permitted`

-- s 63(b): Chapter 6.  No regulations under s 46 (NOTHING): no commencement day, not in force.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences, if section 46 regulations entered into force on` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 6 is in force on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `if section 46 regulations entered into force on` NOTHING
-- Regulations in force before the 18 months are up: the later date governs.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences, if section 46 regulations entered into force on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 1 16)
-- Regulations in force after the 18 months are up: they govern.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences, if section 46 regulations entered into force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 6 is in force on` (YMD 2027 5 31) `if section 46 regulations entered into force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 is in force on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `if section 46 regulations entered into force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))

-- The gap: from when the licensing machinery operates is not stated.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day from which the licensing provisions of sections 6, 8, 9, 16 and 17 operate`

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 2: Definitions`
-- ============================================================================

-- "רישיון דרגה 1 ... עד 18 קילו־ואט": up to, so 18 is covered and above 18 is not.
#ASSERT `s 2: a licence of` `Grade 1` `covers work on a system of cooling output` 18 `kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: a licence of` `Grade 1` `covers work on a system of cooling output` 18.5 `kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s 2: a licence of` `Grade 2` `covers work on a system of cooling output` 70 `kilowatts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: a licence of` `Grade 2` `covers work on a system of cooling output` 70.5 `kilowatts`
#ASSERT `s 2: a licence of` `Grade 3` `covers work on a system of cooling output` 5000 `kilowatts`

-- "תעודת גמר" (1): a Division certificate counts only with an exam passed that included both a
-- theory exam and a practical exam.  This is what the SimpLEX worked example means by "the Law
-- requires passing an exam" -- but it is the definition in s 2, not section 9(a).
--                                 Division  studies  passed   theory   practical  MoE    climate
`a Division certificate, both exams passed`      MEANS Certificate OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a Division certificate, theory exam only`       MEANS Certificate OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Division certificate, no exam passed`         MEANS Certificate OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate` MEANS Certificate OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`a Ministry of Education certificate, studies not completed` MEANS Certificate OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE

#ASSERT `s 2: this is a final certificate` `a Division certificate, both exams passed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: this is a final certificate` `a Division certificate, theory exam only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: this is a final certificate` `a Division certificate, no exam passed`
#ASSERT `s 2: this is a final certificate` `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: this is a final certificate` `a Ministry of Education certificate, studies not completed`

-- "מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר": a purpose of removing heat, by means of a refrigerant.
#ASSERT `s 2: this is a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` (`Refrigeration or air-conditioning system` OF TRUE, TRUE, 15, `an ordinary refrigerant`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: this is a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` (`Refrigeration or air-conditioning system` OF TRUE, FALSE, 15, `an ordinary refrigerant`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2: this is a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` (`Refrigeration or air-conditioning system` OF FALSE, TRUE, 15, `an ordinary refrigerant`)

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 8: The validity of a licence`
-- ============================================================================

-- Reading A (taken, F-V1).  A grant between 1 January and 30 March: the five-year limb is earlier.
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 10
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 3 30) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 30
-- 31 March: the two limbs coincide.
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- Any later grant in the year: 31 March of the fifth year is earlier.
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31

-- Reading B: the 31 March limb is 31 March of the FOURTH year after, and is always the earlier.
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period on the other reading, for a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 31
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period on the other reading, for a licence given on` (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 31
-- ... so under B the five-year limb never decides, which is why A is taken.
#ASSERT `the 31 March limb on the other reading for a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 1) LESS THAN `the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` (YMD 2025 1 1)

-- A renewed validity period is not answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the end of a renewed validity period`

--  grade, began, temporary, last day of a temporary licence, renewal
`a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025`  MEANS Licence OF `Grade 1`, YMD 2025 9 1, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE
`a Grade 3 licence given on 1 September 2025`  MEANS Licence OF `Grade 3`, YMD 2025 9 1, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE
`a renewed Grade 1 licence`                    MEANS Licence OF `Grade 1`, YMD 2030 4 1, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE

#ASSERT `the last day of the validity period of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
#ASSERT `the licence` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2025 8 31)
#ASSERT `the licence` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the validity period of` `a renewed Grade 1 licence`

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 3: The duty to hold a licence`
-- ============================================================================

GIVEN kw IS A NUMBER
      r  IS A Refrigerant
GIVETH A `Refrigeration or air-conditioning system`
`a system of` kw `kilowatts using` r MEANS
    `Refrigeration or air-conditioning system` OF TRUE, TRUE, kw, r

--  system, a First Schedule act, reserved to Grade 3, exempted by an order, the day of the work
`a Grade 3 only act on a system of 60 kilowatts on 1 February 2026` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 60 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2026 2 1
`an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2026 2 1
`an ordinary act on a system of 30 kilowatts on 1 February 2026` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 30 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2026 2 1
`an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts before the Law commenced` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2025 7 15
`an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on an ordinary refrigerant in 2026` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `an ordinary refrigerant`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2026 6 1
`an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on an ordinary refrigerant in 2027` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `an ordinary refrigerant`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2027 2 1
`an act on a system of 15 kilowatts exempted by an order under s 3(b)` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, YMD 2026 2 1
`a cleaning act the First Schedule does not fix` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2026 2 1
`an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts after the licence ran out` MEANS
    `Piece of work` OF (`a system of` 15 `kilowatts using` `a listed flammable refrigerant, use permitted`), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2030 4 1

--  the licence held, acting in accordance with the conditions and the Law
`a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions`     MEANS `Person doing work` OF (JUST `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025`), TRUE
`a person with a Grade 1 licence who breaks its conditions`    MEANS `Person doing work` OF (JUST `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025`), FALSE
`a person with a Grade 3 licence who keeps its conditions`     MEANS `Person doing work` OF (JUST `a Grade 3 licence given on 1 September 2025`), TRUE
`a person with no licence`                                     MEANS `Person doing work` OF NOTHING, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
-- Not work on a system as s 2 defines it (the act is not one the First Schedule fixes).
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `a cleaning act the First Schedule does not fix`
-- s 3(b): the Minister's order.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `an act on a system of 15 kilowatts exempted by an order under s 3(b)`
-- s 63: before the Law commenced for that class of work, nothing is required.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts before the Law commenced`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on an ordinary refrigerant in 2026`
#ASSERT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on an ordinary refrigerant in 2027`

-- Grade 1 covers 15 kilowatts but not 30; Grade 3 covers both, and the Grade 3 only act.
#ASSERT `s 3(a): a licence of` `Grade 1` `is of a type appropriate to` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence of` `Grade 1` `is of a type appropriate to` `an ordinary act on a system of 30 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
#ASSERT `s 3(a): a licence of` `Grade 2` `is of a type appropriate to` `an ordinary act on a system of 30 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): a licence of` `Grade 2` `is of a type appropriate to` `a Grade 3 only act on a system of 60 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
#ASSERT `s 3(a): a licence of` `Grade 3` `is of a type appropriate to` `a Grade 3 only act on a system of 60 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`

#ASSERT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
-- Wrong type for the system.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 30 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
-- Right type, but the conditions of the licence are not kept.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who breaks its conditions` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
-- No licence at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with no licence` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
-- The licence has run out (s 8).
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts after the licence ran out`
-- Nothing required, so an unlicensed person complies.
#ASSERT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with no licence` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts before the Law commenced`
#ASSERT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with no licence` `in` `an act on a system of 15 kilowatts exempted by an order under s 3(b)`
-- Grade 3 only act: Grade 3 complies, Grade 1 does not.
#ASSERT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 3 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `a Grade 3 only act on a system of 60 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `a Grade 3 only act on a system of 60 kilowatts on 1 February 2026`

-- The prohibition as conduct: an unlicensed person who does the work breaches; a licensed one has
-- nothing to breach.
#TRACE `s 3(a): the person must not perform the work` `a person with no licence` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person doing the work` DOES `perform work on the system` AT 5
#TRACE `s 3(a): the person must not perform the work` `a person with a Grade 1 licence who keeps its conditions` `in` `an ordinary act on a system of 15 kilowatts on 1 February 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person doing the work` DOES `perform work on the system` AT 5

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 6: Conditions for giving a licence; the Second Schedule`
-- ============================================================================

-- Prior training and experience, positional:
--   Grade 1 licence, Grade 2 licence, Division certificate, MoE units, technician, practical engineer,
--   mechanical engineer, completed the supplementary programme, years in 3, years in 7
`prior: none`                                        MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: one year of experience in three`             MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1, 1
`prior: three years of experience in seven`          MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 3
`prior: a Division certificate with no grade stated` MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST `a certificate with no grade stated`, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a youth school certificate`                  MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST `a certificate from a vocational youth school of the Division`, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a Grade 1 licence`                           MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF TRUE,  FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a Grade 2 licence`                           MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, TRUE,  NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a Grade 1 Division certificate`              MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST `a Grade 1 certificate`, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a Grade 2 Division certificate`              MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST `a Grade 2 certificate`, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a 3 study unit climate-control certificate`  MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST 3, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate`  MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, JUST 5, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a technician and the supplementary programme` MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  0, 0
`prior: a technician without the programme`          MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a practical engineer and the supplementary programme` MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  0, 0
`prior: a practical engineer without the programme`  MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0
`prior: a mechanical engineer`                       MEANS `Prior training and experience` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, 0, 0

-- Training completed, positional: Grade 1, Grade 2, Grade 3, no grade stated, MoE units obtained
`completed: nothing`            MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`completed: the Grade 1 training` MEANS `Training completed` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`completed: the Grade 2 training` MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
`completed: the Grade 3 training` MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, NOTHING
`completed: the training with no grade stated` MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING
`completed: a 3 study unit climate-control certificate` MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST 3
`completed: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate` MEANS `Training completed` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST 5

-- An applicant who is an adult, a citizen, with no conviction, applying on a day.
GIVEN sought IS A `Licence grade`
      day    IS A DATE
      pr     IS A `Prior training and experience`
      co     IS A `Training completed`
GIVETH AN Applicant
`an ordinary applicant seeking` sought `on` day `with` pr `and` co MEANS
    Applicant OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, sought, day, pr, co

-- ---- Part A: Grade 1 ----------------------------------------------------------

-- Item 1.  No prior training or experience: Grade 1 training of up to 350 hours, OR a 3 unit
-- Ministry of Education certificate.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: a 3 study unit climate-control certificate`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: nothing`)
-- A 5 unit certificate is not the 3 unit one item 1 names.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate`)
#ASSERT `supplementary studies are required of` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: nothing`)

-- Item 2.  Experience: Grade 1 training of up to 220 hours.  Valid three years from the
-- Commencement Day: the last day is 16 July 2028 on the taken reading (F-D3, F-S4).
#ASSERT `the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: one year of experience in three` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: three years of experience in seven` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16) `with` `prior: one year of experience in three` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17) `with` `prior: one year of experience in three` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
-- Experience short of both windows (nothing in the Schedule covers it).
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: three years of experience in seven` `and` `completed: nothing`)

-- Item 3.  A Division certificate with no grade stated: training conferring the certificate with
-- no grade stated.  A Grade 1 training is not that (F-S3).
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Division certificate with no grade stated` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Division certificate with no grade stated` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)

-- ---- Part B: Grade 2 ----------------------------------------------------------

-- Item 1.  None: Grade 2 training of up to 480 hours, OR a 5 unit certificate.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: a 3 study unit climate-control certificate`)
-- A Grade 1 training is not the Grade 2 training the part asks for.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)

-- Item 2.  A registered technician who completed the programme that includes the supplementary
-- course: "בלא דרישות נוספות" -- nothing more is required.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a technician and the supplementary programme` `and` `completed: nothing`)
#ASSERT NOT `supplementary studies are required of` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a technician and the supplementary programme` `and` `completed: nothing`)
-- Item 6.  A registered technician without the programme: training with no grade stated.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a technician without the programme` `and` `completed: nothing`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a technician without the programme` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)

-- Item 3.  A Grade 1 licence, or a Grade 1 certificate, or a 3 unit certificate: Grade 2 training of up to 100 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 1 licence` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 1 Division certificate` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a 3 study unit climate-control certificate` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 1 licence` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)

-- Item 4.  Experience: Grade 2 training of up to 330 hours; a three-year row.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: one year of experience in three` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17) `with` `prior: one year of experience in three` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)

-- Item 5.  A certificate with no grade stated, a youth school certificate, or a 5 unit certificate:
-- training with no grade stated, up to 50 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a youth school certificate` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 2` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Division certificate with no grade stated` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)

-- ---- Part C: Grade 3 ----------------------------------------------------------

-- Item 1.  None: Grade 3 training of up to 720 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 2 training`)

-- Item 2.  A registered practical engineer who completed the programme: nothing more required.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a practical engineer and the supplementary programme` `and` `completed: nothing`)
-- Item 7.  A registered practical engineer without the programme: training with no grade stated.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a practical engineer without the programme` `and` `completed: nothing`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a practical engineer without the programme` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)

-- Item 3.  A Grade 1 licence or certificate or a 3 unit certificate: Grade 3 training of up to 290 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 1 licence` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
-- The applicant who completed only the Grade 1 training does not meet it.
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 1 licence` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
-- Item 4.  A Grade 2 licence or certificate or a 5 unit certificate: Grade 3 training of up to 240 hours.
-- (The gazette has column A and column B apart; the wiki collapses them.  The row is read from the gazette.)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 2 licence` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Grade 2 Division certificate` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a 5 study unit climate-control certificate` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
-- Item 5.  Experience: Grade 3 training of up to 455 hours; a three-year row.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: three years of experience in seven` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17) `with` `prior: three years of experience in seven` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
-- Item 6.  A certificate with no grade stated: training with no grade stated, up to 200 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a Division certificate with no grade stated` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)
-- Item 8.  A registered mechanical engineer: Grade 3 training of up to 230 hours.
#ASSERT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a mechanical engineer` `and` `completed: the Grade 3 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Second Schedule is met by` (`an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 3` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a mechanical engineer` `and` `completed: the training with no grade stated`)

-- ---- s 6(a) as a whole --------------------------------------------------------

`an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training` MEANS
    `an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: the Grade 1 training`
`an applicant who has not done the training` MEANS
    `an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: none` `and` `completed: nothing`

#ASSERT `s 6(a)(1): the applicant is an adult` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training`
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(2): the applicant is an Israeli citizen or a resident of Israel` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training`
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3): no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training`
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(a): the applicant holds a final certificate` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training`
#ASSERT `s 6(a): all the conditions for giving a licence are met by` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a): all the conditions for giving a licence are met by` `an applicant who has not done the training`

-- (1): a minor.  (2): neither a citizen nor a resident.
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a): all the conditions for giving a licence are met by` (Applicant OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a): all the conditions for giving a licence are met by` (Applicant OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
-- (3): a conviction alone does not disqualify; it must be one the Registrar finds makes the
-- applicant unfit, "לדעת הרשם".
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3): no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (Applicant OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(3): no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (Applicant OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: the Grade 1 training`)
-- The Registrar's opinion with no conviction or pending indictment is not a ground.
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3): no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (Applicant OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: the Grade 1 training`)

-- Limb (b), and the fork over how the Schedule qualifies (F-S1): a registered technician with the
-- programme applying for Grade 1.  Part A has no row for a technician, so on the taken reading
-- (the Schedule governs every limb) the conditions fail; on the other reading limb (b) suffices.
`a registered technician applying for Grade 1` MEANS
    `an ordinary applicant seeking` `Grade 1` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` `prior: a technician and the supplementary programme` `and` `completed: nothing`
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4)(b): the applicant is registered in the registry of practical engineers and technicians` `a registered technician applying for Grade 1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 6(a)(4): one of the qualifying conditions, in accordance with the Second Schedule` `a registered technician applying for Grade 1`
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(4) on the other reading: the Schedule qualifies limb (c) only` `a registered technician applying for Grade 1`

-- Renewal: the conditions of s 6 except (a)(4) (s 8).  The applicant who has not done the training
-- may still renew, because the training condition is dropped.
#ASSERT `s 8: the conditions for renewing a licence are met by` `an applicant who has not done the training`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8: the conditions for renewing a licence are met by` (Applicant OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `Grade 1`, YMD 2026 3 1, `prior: none`, `completed: nothing`)

-- "הרשם ייתן": the duty.  Conditions met, no act yet: the standing duty is printed back; performed: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 6(a): the Registrar shall give a licence to` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 3)
#TRACE `s 6(a): the Registrar shall give a licence to` `an applicant who qualifies for Grade 1 by training` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `give the licence to the applicant` AT 10
-- Conditions not met: no duty at all.
#TRACE `s 6(a): the Registrar shall give a licence to` `an applicant who has not done the training` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 3)

