§ `Section 16: The duty to update details`
-- ============================================================================

`a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 30th day, in the manner directed` MEANS
    `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE
`a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 31st day` MEANS
    `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 4 1), TRUE
`a change on 1 March 2026, told in time but not in the manner directed` MEANS
    `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), JUST (YMD 2026 3 10), FALSE
`a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told` MEANS
    `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), NOTHING, TRUE

-- "בתוך 30 ימים מיום השינוי": the last day is the change day plus 30 (F-D4).
#ASSERT `s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 30th day, in the manner directed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 31st day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 1 March 2026, told in time but not in the manner directed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told`
-- Breach only after the last day.
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told`
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told`
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 5) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 31st day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 5) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 30th day, in the manner directed`

-- WITHIN 30 is inclusive: day 30 in time, day 31 a breach.
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 30th day, in the manner directed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `tell the Registrar of the change in details` AT 30
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 1 March 2026, told on the 31st day` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `tell the Registrar of the change in details` AT 31
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 1 March 2026, not yet told` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- ============================================================================
§ `Section 17: Refresher training`
-- ============================================================================

-- A Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025 ends on 31 March 2030 (s 8, reading A), so its
-- last year is 1 April 2029 to 31 March 2030 on the taken reading (F-V3).

--  date, hours, supervised, recognised, field, directed, met requirements
`eight hours on 1 June 2029` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 6 1), 8, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`five hours on 1 June 2029` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 6 1), 5, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`three hours on 1 July 2029` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 7 1), 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`eight hours on the first day of the last year` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 3 31), 8, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`eight hours the day before the last year began` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 3 30), 8, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`eight hours on 1 June 2029, not recognised` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 6 1), 8, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`eight hours on 1 June 2029, requirements not met` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 6 1), 8, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`eight hours on 1 June 2029, outside the field of the licence` MEANS
    `Refresher training attended` OF (YMD 2029 6 1), 8, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029`)
-- At least eight: aggregate across trainings ("בהשתלמויות", plural: F-T2).
#ASSERT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`, `three hours on 1 July 2029`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`)
#ASSERT `s 17(a): the qualifying hours attended by` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`, `three hours on 1 July 2029`) EQUALS 8
-- Only the last year of validity counts (the boundary day is F-V3).
#ASSERT `s 17(a): the training` `eight hours on the first day of the last year` `counts towards the duty of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the training` `eight hours the day before the last year began` `counts towards the duty of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025`
-- A training that is not recognised, or whose requirements were not met, or that is outside the
-- field of the licence, does not count.
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029, not recognised`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029, requirements not met`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029, outside the field of the licence`)
-- No breach until the last day of validity has passed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2030 3 31) `of the duty of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `given` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`)
#ASSERT `s 17(a): the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `of the duty of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `given` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(a): the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `of the duty of` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `given` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029`)

-- (b): the Registrar's requirement, and the Council.
`a requirement with every finding made` MEANS `Additional training requirement` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a requirement without consulting the Council` MEANS `Additional training requirement` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a requirement with no finding of necessity` MEANS `Additional training requirement` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training on` `a requirement with every finding made`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training on` `a requirement without consulting the Council`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training on` `a requirement with no finding of necessity`

-- (c): not more than three months.  `add months` clamps to the end of a shorter month.
#ASSERT `s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30
#ASSERT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `to` (YMD 2030 6 30) `is within the three months allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `to` (YMD 2030 7 1) `is within the three months allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2030 3 31) `to` (YMD 2030 3 30) `is within the three months allowed`

-- (d): the duty is a condition of the licence.
#ASSERT `s 17(d): the conditions of the licence, including the s 17 duty, are met given` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(d): the conditions of the licence, including the s 17 duty, are met given` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(d): the conditions of the licence, including the s 17 duty, are met given` FALSE `and` FALSE

-- (f): published on the website and a reasonable time before.
#ASSERT `s 17(f): the training was published as required` (`Publication of a training` OF TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(f): the training was published as required` (`Publication of a training` OF TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(f): the training was published as required` (`Publication of a training` OF FALSE, TRUE)

-- The duty as conduct.  Eight hours taken: nothing owed.  Five hours: the duty stands, and a
-- trace with no act prints it back; taking part clears it.
#TRACE `s 17(a): the licensee must take part in refresher training` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `eight hours on 1 June 2029`) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)
#TRACE `s 17(a): the licensee must take part in refresher training` `a Grade 1 licence given on 1 September 2025` `in` (LIST `five hours on 1 June 2029`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `take part in refresher training in the last year of the licence` AT 100
#TRACE `s 17(e): the Registrar shall ensure that refresher trainings exist and are available` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)
#TRACE `s 17(f): the Registrar shall publish the refresher trainings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `publish the refresher trainings on the Ministry's website` AT 5

-- ============================================================================
§ `Interpretation Law s 10: how the forward-counted periods are counted`
-- ============================================================================

-- Every period in this encoding that is counted forward from a day goes through the Interpretation
-- row's module.  The values below were decided from s 10 (and the weekday of each nominal last
-- day, checked on a calendar) before the modules were changed; s 10(a): the day "from" which a
-- period of days runs is not counted; s 10(b): a period of months or years after an event ends on
-- the day with the event day's number, or the month's last day, inside the period; s 10(c): a day
-- of rest, recess or holiday counts in a period unless it is one of its LAST days; s 8: "until"
-- includes the day named.  Days of rest are an input: the calendars are in hvac-tests-calendars.l4.

§§ `The statutory counting, with no rest-day input`

-- s 10(b): three years after 16 July 2025 end on 16 July 2028, inside the period; s 8: "until" includes it.
#ASSERT `the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
-- s 10(b): 18 months after 16 July 2025 end on 16 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- s 10(b): three months after 14 January 2025 end on 14 April 2025, which is why the later date, 16 July, decides.
#ASSERT `the Commencement Day` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- s 10(b): five years after 15 January 2025 end on 15 January 2030, earlier than the 31 March limb (31 March 2030).
#ASSERT `the end of the five-year limb for a period beginning on` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
-- s 10(b): one year after 2 January 2026 ends on 2 January 2027, inside the period; the next day is outside.
#ASSERT `s 9: a period from` (YMD 2026 1 2) `to` (YMD 2027 1 2) `does not exceed one year`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9: a period from` (YMD 2026 1 2) `to` (YMD 2027 1 3) `does not exceed one year`
-- s 10(a): thirty days from 5 March 2026 end on 4 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` (`Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 5), NOTHING, TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
-- The temporary licence ceiling is three one-year periods back to back (F-V5): from 10 January 2026, 10 January 2029.
#ASSERT `the latest last day of a temporary licence that began on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2029 1 10
-- A 29 February start: each period clamps to 28 February, and three of them end on 28 February 2031.
#ASSERT `the latest last day of a temporary licence that began on` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2031 2 28

§§ `s 10(c) applied to a deadline for doing something (F-X1): s 16`

-- The change of 4 March 2026 (a Wednesday): thirty days from it end on Friday 3 April 2026.
-- With no rest-day input, or with only Saturday a day of rest, that Friday is the last day; with
-- Friday and Saturday both days of rest it moves to Sunday 5 April 2026.
`a change on 4 March 2026, not yet told` MEANS `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 4), NOTHING, TRUE
-- The change of 5 March 2026 (a Thursday): thirty days from it end on Saturday 4 April 2026, a day
-- of rest under both calendars, so the last day is Sunday 5 April 2026.
`a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` MEANS `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 5), NOTHING, TRUE
`a change on 5 March 2026, told on Sunday 5 April` MEANS `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 5), JUST (YMD 2026 4 5), TRUE
`a change on 5 March 2026, told on Monday 6 April` MEANS `Change of details` OF (YMD 2026 3 5), JUST (YMD 2026 4 6), TRUE

#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 4 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 4 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 4 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 4
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5
#ASSERT (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 5

-- Told on Sunday 5 April: late with no days of rest, in time when Saturday is a day of rest.
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Sunday 5 April`
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Sunday 5 April` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Monday 6 April` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`

-- Breach: from Sunday 5 April with no days of rest; only from Monday 6 April with Saturday a day of rest.
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 5) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told`
#ASSERT NOT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 5) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` (YMD 2026 4 6) `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` `a change on 5 March 2026, not yet told` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`

-- The duty as conduct, counted in days from the day of the change (AT 0 = 5 March): with no days
-- of rest WITHIN 30, so day 31 breaches; with Saturday a day of rest WITHIN 31, so day 31 is in
-- time and day 32 breaches.
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Sunday 5 April` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `tell the Registrar of the change in details` AT 31
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Sunday 5 April` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `tell the Registrar of the change in details` AT 31
#TRACE `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` `a change on 5 March 2026, told on Monday 6 April` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `tell the Registrar of the change in details` AT 32

§§ `s 10(c) applied to a deadline for doing something (F-X1): s 17(c)`

-- A licence whose validity ends on Saturday 31 March 2029: three months after end on Saturday 30 June 2029.
-- A licence whose validity ends on Friday 31 March 2028: three months after end on Friday 30 June 2028.
#ASSERT `s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2029 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 30
#ASSERT (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2029 3 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2029 7 1
#ASSERT (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2029 3 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2029 7 1
#ASSERT `s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2028 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2028 6 30
#ASSERT (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2028 3 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2028 6 30
#ASSERT (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` (YMD 2028 3 31) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 2
-- An extension to Sunday 1 July 2029 is over the ceiling with no days of rest and inside it when
-- Saturday is one; an extension to Monday 2 July is over it either way.
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2029 3 31) `to` (YMD 2029 7 1) `is within the three months allowed`
#ASSERT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2029 3 31) `to` (YMD 2029 7 1) `is within the three months allowed, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 17(c): an extension from` (YMD 2029 3 31) `to` (YMD 2029 7 2) `is within the three months allowed, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`

§§ `s 10(c) NOT applied to a period of validity (F-X2): ss 8, 9 and the Second Schedule`

-- A licence given on Sunday 12 January 2025 (as an illustration): five years after end on
-- Saturday 12 January 2030, before the 31 March limb.  Taken: the validity ends on the 12th.
-- The alternative applies (c) to the five-year limb: the 13th, under either calendar.
`a licence given on 12 January 2025` MEANS Licence OF `Grade 1`, YMD 2025 1 12, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 12) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 12
#ASSERT (`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 12) `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 13
#ASSERT (`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 12) `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 13
#ASSERT `the licence` `a licence given on 12 January 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2030 1 12)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence` `a licence given on 12 January 2025` `is valid on` (YMD 2030 1 13)
-- A grant on Saturday 11 January 2025: five years end on Friday 11 January 2030, which only the
-- Friday-and-Saturday calendar treats as a day of rest (so the alternative moves it to the 13th).
#ASSERT (`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 11) `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 11
#ASSERT (`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 1 11) `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 13
-- "עד 31 במרץ" is a date named, not a period counted, so (c) never reaches it: a grant on 15 June
-- 2025 ends on Sunday 31 March 2030 under every calendar, including one where Sunday is a day of rest.
#ASSERT `the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
#ASSERT (`the last day of the first validity period of a licence given on` (YMD 2025 6 15) `, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Sundays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
-- s 9: one year from 2 January 2026 ends on Saturday 2 January 2027.  Taken: that is the ceiling,
-- and 3 January is over it (asserted above).
-- The Second Schedule's three years end on Sunday 16 July 2028: neither calendar moves it, and a
-- calendar where Sunday is a day of rest would (the alternative function, as an illustration).
#ASSERT (`the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT (`the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT (`the last day of the three-year rows of the Second Schedule, if s 10(c) applied to a period of validity, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Sundays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 17

§§ `s 10(c) NOT applied to a commencement day (F-X3): s 63`

-- Work on any other refrigerant: 18 months after 16 July 2025 end on Saturday 16 January 2027.
-- Taken: the Law commences on that day.  The alternative applies (c): Sunday 17 January 2027.
#ASSERT (`the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using any other refrigerant` `, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
#ASSERT (`the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using any other refrigerant` `, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- The Commencement Day itself (16 July 2025, a Wednesday), and the commencement for listed
-- flammable refrigerants, move under neither calendar.
#ASSERT (`the Commencement Day, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT (`the day the Law commences for` `work on a system using a listed flammable refrigerant whose use is permitted by law` `, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- Reading A of F-C1 (three months after the later of two dates) gives 16 October 2025, a Thursday.
#ASSERT `the Commencement Day on the other reading` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
